      "For a real estate agent or agency, the website is the shop window. Buyers and renters search online first, compare listings on their phones, and contact the agent whose site makes it easiest to find the right property and get an answer. A weak website does not just look bad, it sends your best leads to the portals and to the competitor whose site works better. This guide explains real estate website cost in plain terms: what the site has to do, what listings and portal feeds add to the price, and what a good site should cost in 2026.",
