      "A DIY platform is the right buy when the questions are simple, the volume is low, and someone on your team will actually maintain it. If your customers mostly ask the same ten questions — hours, prices, location, booking — a platform bot can handle them for the price of a lunch a month. It is the wrong buy when nobody owns it: a DIY bot that nobody updates becomes a liability faster than having no bot at all.",
      "A managed chatbot is the right buy when the volume justifies it and you want it done properly without hiring for it. The setup fee pays for the build and the training; the monthly fee pays for the monitoring, the corrections, and the handover. For a hotel, a clinic, a restaurant group, or any business that takes enquiries on WhatsApp around the clock, the maths is usually simple: if the bot saves one missed booking a week, it has paid for itself.",
      "A custom build is the right buy when the chatbot has to do things a platform cannot — check real availability, look up an order, change a booking, talk to your own systems. That is software development with a conversational front end, priced like software development. If a vendor offers you a custom build at a platform price, they are selling you a platform build with a custom label.",
      "## How to tell if a chatbot will pay for itself",
      "Count the conversations you are already losing. How many WhatsApp messages arrive after hours? How many website visitors leave without enquiring? How many calls go unanswered? A chatbot earns its keep in three ways: answering the enquiries that currently get no answer, qualifying the ones that do so your team spends time on buyers instead of browsers, and booking or taking the order while the customer is still interested.",
      "A rough rule: if your business takes more than 20 enquiries a week, and more than a quarter of them arrive outside working hours, a managed chatbot at $299 a month is cheap insurance. If you take fewer than five enquiries a week, a DIY platform is enough, and a managed build would be overkill. The honest answer for a very small business is often that a chatbot is not the next purchase — a better contact page and a WhatsApp button are.",
      "## Frequently asked questions",
      "How much does an AI chatbot cost for a small business?",
      "A DIY platform costs $0–$300 a month. A managed chatbot built and maintained by an agency costs from $999 to set up plus around $299 a month. A custom-built chatbot costs $5,000–$25,000 or more to build, plus hosting and maintenance.",
      "Is a chatbot cheaper than hiring a receptionist?",
      "Yes, by a wide margin, for answering routine questions around the clock. A managed chatbot at $299 a month costs less than a single day of reception cover in most markets. It does not replace a human for complex or sensitive conversations — it filters them, so your team handles the ones that need a person.",
      "What is the difference between a chatbot and an AI calling agent?",
      "A chatbot answers written messages on WhatsApp or your website. An AI calling agent answers phone calls, in voice, including after hours. Many businesses need both: the chatbot for messaging, the calling agent for the calls that still come in by phone. Our guide to AI chatbots for hotels explains the messaging side; our AI receptionist guide covers the cost of missed calls.",
      "Can a chatbot work on WhatsApp?",
      "Yes — WhatsApp is the most common channel for a business chatbot, especially in the UAE, Gulf, Pakistan and India, where customers already message businesses there. It runs through the official WhatsApp Business API, which also carries per-conversation fees from Meta. Unofficial tools that automate the WhatsApp app risk a number ban and should be avoided.",
      "How long does it take to set up a chatbot?",
      "A managed build typically takes two to four weeks: a week to gather your content and answers, a week to build and train, and a week of testing against real customer questions before it goes live. A DIY platform can be live in a day, but the training and testing still take the same time if it is going to answer well.",
      "If your customers are already messaging you after hours, send us the questions they ask most — or just tell us where the messages go unanswered. We will reply within one business day with an honest view of whether a chatbot pays for itself for you, which route fits, and what it would cost. You can also write to us directly at hello@cinem.tech, or explore our AI chatbot service first.",
