      "The mistake is choosing by build price alone. A platform store that costs $3,000 to build and $300 a month in platform and app fees costs $6,600 in year one and $3,600 every year after. A custom store that costs $12,000 to build and $200 a month to host and maintain costs $14,400 in year one and $2,400 a year after. By year three, the custom store is cheaper — and the platform store has paid its app subscriptions every month whether it sold anything or not.",
      "## The costs nobody puts in the quote",
      "Payment fees. Every order pays the payment gateway — typically around 2–3% plus a fixed fee per transaction, depending on the provider and the country. On $10,000 of monthly sales, that is $200–$300 a month, every month, before you have paid for anything else. It is not a hidden fee, but it is the largest ongoing cost of most small stores, and it belongs in the business plan, not in a footnote.",
      "Apps and plugins. The platform store that looks complete on day one usually needs paid apps for the second month: reviews, search, discounts, email, shipping rules, each $5–$50 a month. App creep is the quiet budget killer of platform stores — audit the subscriptions every quarter, and cancel anything the store has outgrown.",
